#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Writes the Slime King's ChatGPT/Gemini prompts for the hit, death and dodge sheets (2026-11-11), modelled on the Elite's (Animations/EliteSlime/source/write_prompts.py) with the King's blocks. The idle prompt was written by
hand (idle/source/slime_king_idle_prompt.txt) and its sheet came out excellent, so the same tone and numbers are used: small body motions, the crown rigid, the glove and staff ONE rigid piece with a gap to the body.

  python Animations/SlimeKing/source/write_prompts.py

Output: Animations/SlimeKing/<folder>/source/<folder>_prompt.txt (the user pastes the text between the two lines of equals signs into ChatGPT, or Gemini, with Animations/SlimeKing/reference_image.png attached).
"""
import os

ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), "..", "..", ".."))

CHARACTER = """CHARACTER: the exact same character as in the attached reference image: the SLIME KING, in exactly the painted look of the reference. A low dome of warm ivory (#F5E5C8, cream shadows), wider than tall, heavy and soft, with a flat skirt-like base that spreads on the floor in six rounded scallops like the folds of a royal robe. A thin dark warm-brown outline around everything. The face: calm, smug and regal, half-lidded gold-amber eyes with heavy lids, soft brows, a gentle confident closed smile, as in the reference. A GOLDEN CROWN with five points, one big red ruby and several small blue sapphires, sitting on top of the dome and tilted a little to the right. On the right, beside the face, a white GLOVE with a gold cuff FLOATS in the air holding a tall GOLDEN STAFF upright, tilted a little towards the right: a twisted golden shaft with rings and small blue sapphires, an ornate golden head of curled leaves with a red ruby in its collar, a big pale cream-gold faceted crystal on top and a small golden spike at the lower end. There is a clear gap between the glove and the body, and nothing joins them or joins the staff to the body or the skirt. No legs, no arms, no cape, no robe, no beard, no ears, no horns, no teeth. Keep the same painted style, colours, crown, staff and face. Do not redesign anything."""

VIEW = """VIEW: the same three-quarter view as in the reference, the whole body and the face turned about 30 degrees towards the RIGHT edge of the panel, as if looking at an enemy standing on the right. The view does not change in any panel: the face never turns away, and it stays in the same place on the body (the body LEANS, it does not turn)."""

SOFT = """NO SOFT EFFECTS: the reference has no halo, glow, rays, sparkles, dust or smoke and neither does any panel: no halo, no glow, no light rays, no sparkles, no bloom, no blur, no dust clouds, no smoke, no mist, no haze, no sparks, no see-through anything, no gradient fade-outs, no light spilling onto the background. NO motion lines, NO smear, NO afterimages, NO speed streaks, NO impact stars, NO shockwave rings, NO cracks drawn on the floor. Every part has a hard, clean, opaque edge. No shadow on the floor, no puddle (unless a sheet says the body itself melts into one), no cast shadow, no shadow ellipse under a body that is in the air. The game adds all light, dust and impact effects later."""

LESSONS = """LESSONS FROM THE EARLIER SHEETS (docs/MONSTERS.md, docs/SLIME_KING.md): (1) The King's idle sheet came out excellent from ChatGPT, which kept the size, the floor and the spacing: ask for a SMALL creature with lots of empty space and a margin round every part that sticks out (the crown tips, the staff tip, the glove). (2) THE GENERATOR EXAGGERATES BODY MOTION two to three times: the numbers below are small on purpose. (3) THE GLOVE AND THE STAFF MUST NOT TOUCH THE BODY OR THE SKIRT: keep a clear gap of flat magenta in every panel unless a pose says otherwise. (4) The face may change a little from panel to panel: that is fine, but it is always the King's calm smug face unless the pose says otherwise."""

BACKGROUND = """BACKGROUND AND LAYOUT: one flat pure MAGENTA (#FF00FF) background filling the whole image, identical in every pixel. No gradient, floor, ground line, shadow, glow or vignette. NO GRID LINES, NO BORDERS and no lines between or around the panels. No text, numbers or labels. No pink, magenta or purple on the creature itself; its outline is dark warm brown and hard-edged."""

RIGID = """THE CROWN, THE GLOVE AND THE STAFF ARE HARD: the crown, the glove and the golden staff never bend, grow, shrink or flicker: they are the same shapes at the same size in every panel (the crown with its five points, its ruby and its sapphires; the staff the same straight shaft, the same length, the same jewels) and the crown only rides with the body when it leans or moves{extra}. The glove and the staff are ONE rigid piece with a clear gap of flat magenta to the body AND to the skirt in every panel (no arm, no stalk, no wrist); it only changes place and turns as one piece."""

REPLIES = """- Replies if it goes wrong. {specific}If it draws a halo, glow, rays, sparkles, dust, smoke, motion lines or impact stars: "Redo it. NO halo, NO glow, NO rays, NO sparkles, NO dust, NO smoke, NO motion lines, NO impact stars: only crisp solid shapes with a thin outline, one position per panel." If the glove is joined to the body or grows an arm: "Redo it. The glove has NO arm, NO stalk and NO wrist: it floats with a clear gap of flat magenta between it and the body in every panel." If the staff touches the skirt or the body: "Redo it. The golden staff touches nothing but the glove: a clear gap of flat magenta between the whole staff and the body and the skirt along its full height." If the glove or staff changes size or bends: "Redo it. The glove and the staff are ONE rigid piece, the same in every panel (same glove, same straight staff, same length, same jewels); only its place and angle change." If the crown changes or slides on the body (unless this sheet says it falls): "Redo it. The crown is solid gold and exactly the same in every panel (five points, the ruby and the sapphires); it only leans with the body as one piece." If the body squashes or stretches like jelly: "Redo it. The King is a heavy, soft ivory lump: the dome keeps its shape and its width; it only rises or lowers a few percent and LEANS, pivoting on its base." If the creature is too big or any part touches a panel edge or reaches into the next panel: "Redo it. The creature is much SMALLER: its base is only about 40% of the panel's width, with lots of empty magenta all round, so that every part, the crown tips and the staff tip included, is at least 10% of the panel away from every panel edge." If the background is not magenta or the creature has pink on it: "Redo it. The background is one flat pure magenta (#FF00FF), identical in every pixel, and nothing on the creature is pink, magenta or purple." If it turns pure white, grey or smooth: "Redo it. Keep the warm ivory body (#F5E5C8) and the thin dark warm-brown outline of the attached picture." If it draws more or fewer panels than asked: "Redo it. EXACTLY the number of panels listed, in the grid listed, nothing in an extra place." """

ANIMS = []

