    what="""WHAT IT IS. The King is struck on the front of its body by the enemy (the warrior, off-screen to the right): the smug smile drops into a grimace, its eyes screw shut, the heavy ivory body rocks back on its base, the crown rides with the dome, the floating glove with the staff is jolted up and back, then everything swings forward past upright, wobbles and settles back to the resting pose. It plays in place on the floor (a hit never moves the monster across the stage; the page adds the white flash and a small shove, so no flash and no impact star is drawn).""",
