    check="(1) the same King in panel 1, then the melt: the crown slipping and the dome sagging (2), the crown tumbling and the staff falling (3), a low mound with the crown on the floor and the staff leaning or lying (4), a wide low puddle (5), the lowest widest puddle with the crown resting on its edge and the staff lying on the floor beside it (6); (2) the centre stays on the same spot, the floor line is the same in every panel, every piece rests on the floor line except the crown and the staff in the middle of their fall (panel 3); (3) the face: grimace and shut eyes in 1, closed eyes with a faint smile in 2 to 4, a faint closed-eye smile on the puddle in 5, none or very faint in 6; (4) the ivory stays the same warm ivory with the thin outline (it melts, it does not turn grey or glow); (5) the crown keeps its shape, gold, ruby and sapphires, and lands on the floor; the staff keeps its shape and its jewels and ends lying on the floor; (6) crisp opaque, no halo, no glow, no flash, no gore; (7) the same size scale in all panels, every piece at least 8% of the panel from every edge; (8) no GIF and no extra images.",
